@@ -273,7 +273,7 @@ Forms keep their own state, so a rename that repaired a source the open node's c
 
 A rename that updated references or left something to review shows a notice titled "Renamed <old> to <new>". It appears above the canvas and, while the node dialog is open, at the top of the dialog too, like the draft conflict notice. It counts the updated references and connections, and says that plain text, JSON values and scripts are not changed. It then lists the places where the old id may remain as the issue badge's rows (Warning, `NODE_REFERENCE_UNCERTAIN`, message, node and path). These are dynamic or computed keys, output keys that an authored patch may own, sources the domain could not verify, and scripts and generated patches. A row on a node still in the draft opens that node's editor at the field (in place for the open node). Loop-level rows only inform. "Undo reverses the whole rename." The notice stays until it is dismissed, the rename is undone or redone, another rename replaces it, or the editor loads again. A rename that only moved connections shows nothing, as before. There is no preview step; Undo is the way back. A computed key could name any node, so every rename lists it.
 
-The persistent reference diagnostics come from the same local `domain` validation as other issues, on node badges and beside Publish. A known missing gate or visit count is an error (`NODE_REFERENCE_MISSING`), and Publish refuses with it. Direct existence checks (`NODE_REFERENCE_OPTIONAL_MISSING`), unverified output keys (`NODE_REFERENCE_OUTPUT_UNVERIFIED`) and dynamic reads (`NODE_REFERENCE_UNCERTAIN`) are warnings. Regression: `editor/store.rename.test.ts` and `editor/EditorPage.rename.test.tsx`.
+The persistent reference diagnostics come from the same local `domain` validation as other issues, on node badges and beside Publish. A known missing gate or visit count is an error (`NODE_REFERENCE_MISSING`), and Publish refuses with it. Direct existence checks (`NODE_REFERENCE_OPTIONAL_MISSING`), unverified output keys (`NODE_REFERENCE_OUTPUT_UNVERIFIED`) and dynamic reads (`NODE_REFERENCE_UNCERTAIN`) are warnings. A rename made while the loop's name is refused (see "Loop names" below) stays on this device with the other held edits; the save that follows a new name sends the whole renamed draft once. Regression: `editor/store.rename.test.ts`, `editor/EditorPage.rename.test.tsx` and Edge `e2e/rename-references.spec.ts` (the Starter's sibling Liquid and Exit through undo, redo, reload, publish and pinned runs; uncertain, optional and missing references with Publish; focus through the remount; held input; a stale tab; protected voice steps).
 
